      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SALSA (8) flew the lids with a fast early split and led until late but gathered in when a 4.5 lengths second at Q Parklands over 520m in 29.98. Speedy runner who can find the front with a clear break from out wide. Good form should continue. BAREFOOT RAVEN (1) goes very well this course and distance starting nine times for three wins and five minors. In the money last time at this track (22.18) in a Grade 5, finishing a 7 length third. Looks suited here and can measure up. GEORGIE'S WONDER (2) failed to feature last start at this track, but prior to that won comfortably by 7 lengths at this track (19.73) beating Messy Tessy in a Grade 6 on September 8. Has the ability to give this a shake. CAMBLA DIVA (6) missed out after being heavily supported last time but can improve.",
